**Company Profile**

Morgan Stanley is a leading global financial services firm providing a wide range of investment banking, securities, investment management and wealth management services. The Firm's employees serve clients worldwide including corporations, governments and individuals from more than 747 offices in 42 countries


As a market leader, the talent and passion of our people is critical to our success. Together, we share a common set of values rooted in integrity, excellence and strong team ethic. Morgan Stanley can provide a superior foundation for building a professional career \\- a place for people to learn, to achieve and grow. A philosophy that balances personal lifestyles, perspectives and needs is an important part of our culture.


**Department Profile**

Morgan Stanley has earned a strong reputation for the originality of its research and the value it creates among investors and decision makers. Our Equity Research team was ranked No.1 for the seventh consecutive year in the Institutional Investor Asia Research Team ranking this year. Our analysts look at economic, market, industry and company data to enhance the performance of clients' global portfolios and to help companies set their strategic direction.


**Primary responsibilities:**

* Update earnings models;
* Contribute to healthcare team’s periodicals, e.g. weekly;
* Summarize and take notes during earnings and business update calls;
* Update marketing materials;
* Write stock\\-specific reports and contribute to thematic research;
* Collect data for thematic research;
* Write up pre\\-deal reports and update pre\\-deal models;
* Participate in client calls and marketing.

**Qualifications:**

* Bachelor's degree; advanced graduate degree a plus (MBA, Master of Science, or above);
* Healthcare/scientific background preferable, via academic degree or work experience;
* Modeling and valuation skills;
* Strong work ethic and discipline;
* Ability to work collaboratively;
* Ability to work long hours;
* Ability to manage multiple projects under tight deadlines.

**WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM MORGAN STANLEY:**

We are committed to maintaining the first\\-class service and high standard of excellence that have defined Morgan Stanley for over 89 years. Our values \\- putting clients first, doing the right thing, leading with exceptional ideas, committing to diversity and inclusion, and giving back \\- aren’t just beliefs, they guide the decisions we make every day to do what's best for our clients, communities and more than 80,000 employees in 1,200 offices across 42 countries. At Morgan Stanley, you’ll find an opportunity to work alongside the best and the brightest, in an environment where you are supported and empowered. Our teams are relentless collaborators and creative thinkers, fueled by their diverse backgrounds and experiences. We are proud to support our employees and their families at every point along their work\\-life journey, offering some of the most attractive and comprehensive employee benefits and perks in the industry. There’s also ample opportunity to move about the business for those who show passion and grit in their work.


To learn more about our offices across the globe, please copy and paste https://www.morganstanley.com/about\\-us/global\\-offices into your browser.


Morgan Stanley is an equal opportunities employer. We work to provide a supportive and inclusive environment where all individuals can maximize their full potential. Our skilled and creative workforce is comprised of individuals drawn from a broad cross section of the global communities in which we operate and who reflect a variety of backgrounds, talents, perspectives, and experiences. Our strong commitment to a culture of inclusion is evident through our constant focus on recruiting, developing, and advancing individuals based on their skills and talents.

**Overview** 










 With a continued growth in the region, a corporate bank is seeking to hire a
 **AVP, Credit Officer, Corporate Credit** 
 to join the Risk Management department to review and recommend
 **Large corporate credit** 
 transactions

 for approval and maintain a healthy and high credit portfolio for the bank.










**Role Responsibilities** 









* Responsible for day\\-to\\-day management of credit risk arising from exposures booked in Corporate Banking;
* Review and approve credit lending proposals within delegated authority to ensure that the bank’s credit offering is in compliance with bank’s policies, procedures and risk appetite;
* Provide recommendations and highlight key risk issues to front office and Head of Credit;
* Stay on top of high alert to credit worthiness of clients including market situations, provide advice to the related departments on proper credit\\-related actions whenever necessary
* Perform on\\-site credit due diligence by joining joint\\-calls with business unit officers;
* Provide training and guidance to RMs / ARMs on credit policies and processes;
* Prepare portfolio reports / analysis of bank’s credit portfolio;
* Participate in credit policy / new product programme review and ad\\-hoc projects assigned by Management;









**Requirements** 









* University graduate in Finance, Economics, Risk Management or related disciplines;
* Holder of ECF\\-CRM is a plus;
* At least 5 years of relevant experience in commercial / corporate banking with credit assessment experience, broad industry exposure and knowledge of cash flow lending;
* Sound knowledge in various corporate lending products Bachelor degree holder or above, preferably in Finance, Banking or Economics related disciplines
* Independent, attentive to details, good analytical and problem\\-solving skills
* Capability to discuss and guide front offices from early stage of deals to make appropriate credit decision
* Strong analytical, communication and interpersonal skills with good command of both spoken and written English and Chinese









 If you believe you have the relevant skill and experience and is interested in this position, kindly get in touch with Jack Leung with your CV and to engage in a confidential discussion.
